# Working Codabench compute worker for competition 2469, verified 2026-08-27.
#
# Every PUBLISHED tag of codalab/competitions-v2-compute-worker is broken against
# the current server, in two separate places:
#
#   1. cpu1.1 (2024-08-05, the tag the EB-NeRD README pins) echoes the submission
#      secret back as Kombu's serialized UUID dict -> server 500s on every status
#      update, and Celery acks on delivery, so the submission is silently lost.
#      latest (v1.22) gets a real uuid.UUID and dies in run_wrapper's own log line:
#      TypeError: Object of type UUID is not JSON serializable.
#
#   2. EB-NeRD is a result-only competition, so no program runs, so output/ is
#      never created -- and push_output opens output/metadata unconditionally:
#      FileNotFoundError: .../output/metadata. It dies just before uploading
#      prediction_result.zip, so the scoring phase then retries forever for a file
#      that was never produced.
#
# Upstream develop fixes both. Mounting develop's file directly does NOT work: it
# needs Python 3.10+ (calls a staticmethod object directly) and these images ship
# Python 3.9. So patch_worker.py ports the two fixes into the released file.
FROM codalab/competitions-v2-compute-worker:latest
COPY patch_worker.py /patch_worker.py
RUN python3 /patch_worker.py
